{
  "_about": "CU-164 (D-94): the player from Ocular Stride. Boots where Stride has that surface (concrete, glass, metal, wood, water). Boots have no dirt, mud, leaves or grass, so packed dirt and the run are generic gravel and leaves are generic grass, and the why says so. Sound rule: immersive, except the landing, which is impactful. A step is one take, cut short so it can repeat. Not picked, because the packs do not have the thing and Jerry's take is the better one: mud (no squelch), jump and the roll and the vault (no gear and no hands), the swim stroke (the packs' water is the sea or a boot splash), breath and both hurts (no soldier's voice; Foundation's breaths are designed and several seconds), and every builds folder (no hammer, sandbag, drill, wire, door, mine beep or spike; Utility's wood is a piece set on a desk, Foundation's hits are trailer booms). Claude makes these; Jerry's ear decides.",
